# GLOBAL COMPLETION RULES FOR ALL PHASES

These rules apply throughout the project.

## Rule 1 — Never break existing phases

Before modifying any file, inspect how it is used.

If a component is shared, update it carefully and check every page that uses it.

## Rule 2 — One shared database

All modules must use the same participant, event, gallery, venue, verification, winner and stream records.

No duplicate databases.

No duplicate business logic.

## Rule 3 — One design system

Every page must use the official wedding design tokens.

Do not invent a different design for registration, verification or admin.

## Rule 4 — No fake functionality

Do not create buttons that do nothing.

Do not create fake charts.

Do not create static participant tables pretending to be database-driven.

Do not claim an upload works unless the file is actually uploaded and saved.

Do not simulate a successful lucky draw without a real backend operation.

## Rule 5 — Preserve actual project details

Do not invent:

- Couple names.
- Wedding dates.
- Venue addresses.
- Personal story content.
- Contact information.
- Photographs.
- YouTube links.

Use editable placeholders where information is missing.

## Rule 6 — Database first for critical functionality

Registration, verification, lucky draw and administrative operations must use real backend logic.

The browser must not be trusted with privileged operations.

## Rule 7 — Premium quality on every screen

Do not spend all the design effort on the homepage.

The registration page, QR verification screen, winners page, live page and admin dashboard must all receive the same attention to detail.

## Rule 8 — Phase completion and handoff

At the end of each phase, report:

1. Features completed.
2. Files created.
3. Files modified.
4. Database changes.
5. API changes.
6. Design components created.
7. Tests performed.
8. Known issues.
9. Dependencies for the next phase.

Do not start the next phase until the current phase has passed its acceptance criteria.

